# UI Dashboard Rules

- Prefer custom per-project visual direction after inspecting current brand and components.
- Avoid generic AI-looking dashboards.
- Reuse existing design tokens, spacing, typography, cards, tables, dialogs, and form controls.
- Dashboard pages should handle loading, empty, error, and permission states.
- CRUD screens should include search/filter when data volume justifies it, not by default.
- Dense admin tables are acceptable for internal operations; keep primary actions obvious.
- Parent/student-facing screens should be friendly, clear, and low-friction.
